entry.summary:
Fast code that crashes on 1 million inputs because it's eating all the RAM is still broken code. That's space complexity. It measures how much memory an algorithm uses relative to input size — expressed in Big-O notation. The extra memory beyond the input — variables, arrays, recursion stack. function sum(arr) { let total = 0; // 1 variable, regardless of arr size for (let x of arr) total += x; return total; }
function copyArray(arr) { return [...arr]; // New array grows with input }
function factorial(n) { if (n === 1) return 1; return n * factorial(n - 1); // n frames on call stack }
Approach Time Space
Caching results O(1) lookup O(n) storage
Recalculating O(n) O(1)
In-place sort Same O(1)
Merge sort O(n log n) O(n) extra
Always state both complexities: "O(n) time and O(1) space" — this shows complete thinking. Part 5 of the Bitveen DSA Series. Originally published at bitveen.com
